What you write is true Phil, but Babel provides an interface to easily
switch between languages.  At the lowest level it also gives you the
opportunity to simply list the languages for which you have
hyphenation patterns in a file, which is processed at iniTeX time.

And babel can also be used with formats other than LaTeX, although
everybody seems to think it is meant only for LaTeX users. I try to
keep it compatible with all plain based formats.

